WEBVTT

00:00:01.210 --> 00:00:03.350
Previously on Battlestar Galactica

00:00:03.910 --> 00:00:05.510
Now you're telling me you're a machine

00:00:05.760 --> 00:00:06.400
A robot

00:00:06.400 --> 00:00:09.180
You knew I wanted access to the defense, mate, Frank

00:00:09.180 --> 00:00:12.740
Do you have any idea what they do to me if they find out?

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:13.530
Get down

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.430
Moments ago, this ship received word

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:20.380
of a Cylon attack against our home worlds is underway

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.140
As of this moment, we are at war

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:26.220
Alright, we can take three more people

00:00:26.220 --> 00:00:27.440
Give it up, I see

00:00:33.520 --> 00:00:38.340
No, I've decided you want an expression of my subconscious mind playing itself out during my waking states.

00:00:38.830 --> 00:00:41.130
So, um, only in your head?

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:44.850
No!

00:00:45.050 --> 00:00:48.030
There may be Cylon agents living among us.

00:00:48.130 --> 00:00:50.170
Some may not even know they're Cylons at all.

00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:54.900
They could be sleeper agents programmed to perfectly impersonate human beings in teleactivation.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:30.640
10 minutes a month.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.020
Plan, plan for everything and everyone.

00:02:28.840 --> 00:02:29.840
Gaius, even

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:30.760
listening to me.

00:02:36.600 --> 00:02:38.040
Passengers, 30 seconds to Mars.

00:02:38.200 --> 00:02:41.020
Planted, men, women, age.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:41.910
You know what?

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:43.360
Do this after the jump.

00:02:43.500 --> 00:02:43.800
It's all right.

00:02:43.800 --> 00:02:44.520
Yes, ma'am, President.

00:02:57.920 --> 00:02:58.200
Yeah.

00:03:02.040 --> 00:03:04.140
I believe in a world I can and do understand.

00:03:04.700 --> 00:03:06.330
A rational universe.

00:03:06.770 --> 00:03:08.720
Playing through rational means.

00:03:10.940 --> 00:03:18.180
You're not rational.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:26.680
No, but you're not rational.

00:03:30.160 --> 00:03:31.180
I wasn't already here.

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:40.380
Madam President, ladies and gentlemen, our 33 minutes are almost up once again.

00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:43.190
Please prepare for our faster-than-light jump. Thank you.

00:03:50.610 --> 00:03:52.350
Getting it all up close this time, aren't we, Billy?

00:03:53.410 --> 00:03:55.390
I thought they'd have to reboot the FTL computer again.

00:04:00.410 --> 00:04:02.510
Why do the silence come every 33 minutes?

00:04:02.830 --> 00:04:04.850
Why isn't it 34, 35?

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:05.270
Charlie.

00:04:05.610 --> 00:04:05.890
What?

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:08.010
Shut up.

00:04:12.840 --> 00:04:13.260
Seconds.

00:04:15.510 --> 00:04:17.350
Sir, jump 237 underway.

00:04:17.930 --> 00:04:19.030
53 ships have jumped.

00:04:19.310 --> 00:04:22.670
10 still reporting trouble with their FDL drives, including Colonial 1.

00:04:23.860 --> 00:04:24.800
We're getting slower.

00:04:27.950 --> 00:04:28.890
Maybe this time.

00:04:51.880 --> 00:04:52.280
Thank you.

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.540
I've got another idea for the next cycle.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:04.460
Ladies and gentlemen, I'm afraid the Cylons have appeared again.

00:05:04.660 --> 00:05:08.300
However, our FTL drive is now working and we will jump momentarily.

00:05:10.240 --> 00:05:11.360
Five days now.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:17.050
The limits.

00:05:19.010 --> 00:05:19.650
The human body.

00:05:19.930 --> 00:05:20.720
The human mind.

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:23.690
This is that you can't push beyond.

00:05:27.040 --> 00:05:27.640
Well, those are facts.

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:35.030
Provable facts. Everyone has the limit.

00:05:36.480 --> 00:05:38.680
You know the drill, people. Scatter formation.

00:05:40.540 --> 00:05:42.380
Don't stray beyond the recovery line.

00:05:47.610 --> 00:05:50.670
Ammo hoisting the main guns. You've got a red light right there.

00:05:55.050 --> 00:05:56.490
We have a hit on the starboard bow.

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.100
Away the damage control parties.

00:05:58.820 --> 00:05:59.920
Base stars launching Raiders.

00:06:19.260 --> 00:06:20.480
Ships away, including Colonial One.

00:06:21.090 --> 00:06:23.170
Recover fighters, stand by to jump.

00:06:23.530 --> 00:06:24.450
Combat landings.

00:06:31.720 --> 00:06:32.580
All fighters aboard, sir.

00:06:32.990 --> 00:06:33.670
Execute jump.

00:06:52.040 --> 00:06:53.680
Jump 237. Complete.

00:06:56.150 --> 00:06:58.090
All civilian ships present and accounted for, sir.

00:06:58.620 --> 00:06:59.420
Start the clock.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:02.270
And let's start prepping for the next Jamba.

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:04.010
Clock is running.

00:07:04.940 --> 00:07:06.560
33 minutes mark.

00:07:12.840 --> 00:07:14.000
You got 32 minutes, people.

00:07:39.080 --> 00:07:40.060
You know you're not safe.

00:07:42.330 --> 00:07:43.090
No, of course not.

00:07:44.750 --> 00:07:46.790
The sidearmers will follow us again,

00:07:47.030 --> 00:07:50.300
as they have the last 237 times.

00:07:53.490 --> 00:07:54.930
You're right, you know, there are limits.

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:58.060
Eventually you'll make a mistake.

00:07:58.320 --> 00:07:59.160
And then you'll kill us all.

00:08:00.510 --> 00:08:06.340
Yes. Yes, I know, but for another 33 minutes.

00:09:36.080 --> 00:09:37.760
I'm gonna try something new this time.

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:47.030
Provide the fleet and the six groups.

00:09:49.380 --> 00:09:52.830
When they jump, we jump two more times,

00:09:52.910 --> 00:09:56.840
and on the fourth jump, we rendezvous at a common set of coordinates.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:09:59.870
24 jumps.

00:10:00.030 --> 00:10:09.370
plot breaking our humps calculating one jump every 33 minutes get up my jacket are you eating this

00:10:12.760 --> 00:10:20.170
combat landings expected again to be the uh order of the day so double check your undercarriage

00:10:20.190 --> 00:10:29.840
before uh look you've all done this 237 times

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:38.060
You know what to do. No mistakes, and let's make it to 238.

00:10:41.210 --> 00:10:42.670
Then good luck, and be careful out there.

00:11:02.810 --> 00:11:05.650
Hey, you do me a favor. Tell Captain Apollo he owes me one wing.

00:11:09.060 --> 00:11:13.180
No, Callie, there's three. I know there's three. Can you check it again for me, please?

00:11:13.440 --> 00:11:13.560
Yeah.

00:11:14.560 --> 00:11:16.420
Please get somebody starting to work.

00:11:17.120 --> 00:11:18.860
Hey, we'll sleep when we're dead. Come on.

00:11:20.020 --> 00:11:20.320
Boomer.

00:11:22.350 --> 00:11:25.930
The latest, the Cylons look like us now. Primary fuel?

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.710
Primary fuel, 2893 KRG.

00:11:29.110 --> 00:11:29.970
Marine told one of the...

00:11:30.090 --> 00:11:34.530
pilots that we marooned some guy back on Ragnar because the XO thought that he was a silent.

00:11:34.690 --> 00:11:39.940
You know what? I don't give a frack. Red light in the number four thruster. Go make a visual ID,

00:11:40.060 --> 00:11:59.630
see if it's blocked. A little rough on the new ACL, you think?

00:12:00.410 --> 00:12:01.270
It's not my ECO.

00:12:01.960 --> 00:12:04.880
It's some refugee from Triton that I've been saddled with, and I didn't ask you.

00:12:10.860 --> 00:12:11.980
Helo's gone, Sharon.

00:12:12.180 --> 00:12:13.200
I didn't ask you that either.

00:12:19.180 --> 00:12:19.540
Sorry.

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:24.470
Morning.

00:12:25.020 --> 00:12:27.060
Sagittarian, how many have you got?

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:29.680
5,251 survivors from Sagittarius.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:37.050
We can't transmit photos yet, so if you want you can leave them here with us or you can put them on the board outside

00:12:42.120 --> 00:12:42.400
Next

00:13:30.830 --> 00:13:31.670
Update on the headcount.

00:13:42.100 --> 00:13:43.200
How did we lose 300?

00:13:44.680 --> 00:13:51.130
There were some overcounts, a few deaths from wounds, and a few missing during the last attack.

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:35.350
We think about that for a minute.

00:14:37.900 --> 00:14:38.140
No.

00:14:41.850 --> 00:14:43.930
Procreation is one of God's commandments.

00:14:44.980 --> 00:14:45.280
Really?

00:14:48.070 --> 00:14:52.490
Someday, if you could sign on, he'll reward you with a lovely little walking toaster of your very own.

00:14:53.920 --> 00:14:56.300
I want us to have a child, guys.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.420
You can't be serious.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:14:59.980
It's Doctor...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:13.440
Amarac. What was that? Um, so sorry for interrupting you while you were speaking. You were just saying?

00:15:14.770 --> 00:15:22.640
Oh, I was just saying that Dr. Amarac had requested to speak with the president. Dr. Amarac, I see.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.760
You know, have you always been able to multitask like this? Yes, yes.

00:15:30.250 --> 00:15:32.010
I used to work with him at the Ministry of Defense.

00:15:34.040 --> 00:15:37.220
It says here that he's uncovered important information

00:15:37.220 --> 00:15:40.210
regarding how the Cylons were able to defeat Claude Defenses.

00:15:41.360 --> 00:15:43.180
I was always a little worried he was on to us.

00:15:43.300 --> 00:15:43.660
Were you?

00:15:44.320 --> 00:15:46.560
Going to speak to him, perhaps I should speak to him if you're busy.

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:50.560
Actually, I think he wanted to speak directly with the president.

00:15:52.010 --> 00:15:52.530
Sound urgent?

00:15:54.810 --> 00:15:56.250
Must be very, very important.

00:15:58.040 --> 00:15:59.980
Maybe something about a certain traitor in the president's...

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:04.740
center circle? There's not enough time before we jump. I want him on board first thing during

00:16:04.740 --> 00:16:22.840
the next cycle. Oh, thank you, doctor. I'd say you have a serious problem. If I can help. He's a strange one, isn't he?

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:03.000
12 more cases of nervous exhaustion.

00:18:03.060 --> 00:18:03.800
They make 61.

00:18:04.180 --> 00:18:08.520
Have the doc start pumping them up with stimulants.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.040
Getting them back on the line.

00:18:10.520 --> 00:18:11.120
Pilots, too.

00:18:11.300 --> 00:18:11.860
He's still in the park.

00:18:12.040 --> 00:18:14.330
One out of every three, every other cycle.

00:18:15.060 --> 00:18:16.480
to come back and bite us in the ass.

00:18:16.720 --> 00:18:19.990
Yeah, well, we have too much work, and I don't know people to do it.

00:18:20.150 --> 00:18:20.510
Fuel report.

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:23.380
I already signed one of these.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:24.080
Yes, sir.

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:24.560
Sorry, sir.

00:18:24.700 --> 00:18:26.400
Con traffic, two from the president.

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.960
Is this my 10 minutes, or is this yours?

00:18:29.240 --> 00:18:29.500
Yours.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:30.700
I took ten last night.

00:18:30.800 --> 00:18:34.030
See you guys in combat.

00:18:35.850 --> 00:18:36.870
It was your ten minutes?

00:18:37.030 --> 00:18:39.370
If the old man's so tired he can't remember, then it's his turn.

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:48.030
Hey, you see the note from the XO?

00:18:48.150 --> 00:18:49.310
Yeah, I saw it. No way.

00:18:49.530 --> 00:18:52.470
Kara, everyone else...

00:18:52.470 --> 00:18:53.730
I don't fly with stims.

00:18:53.730 --> 00:18:55.960
A bunch of reflexes, your reaction time.

00:18:56.240 --> 00:18:58.880
Come on, Kara, give me a break.

00:18:59.000 --> 00:18:59.320
Just...

00:18:59.320 --> 00:18:59.980
Why are we...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.000
arguing about this.

00:19:02.044 --> 00:19:03.084
I have no idea.

00:19:03.204 --> 00:19:04.944
Neither do I. You're the CAG. Act like one.

00:19:05.212 --> 00:19:06.172
What the hell does that mean?

00:19:07.900 --> 00:19:10.780
It means that you're still acting like you're everyone's best friend.

00:19:11.036 --> 00:19:12.536
We're not friends, you're the king.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:14.760
Be careful out there.

00:19:15.420 --> 00:19:19.260
Our job isn't to be careful, it's to shoot silence out of the frackin' sky.

00:19:19.516 --> 00:19:21.056
Good hunting is what you say.

00:19:21.532 --> 00:19:25.472
And now one of your idiot pilots is acting like a child and refusing to take her pills.

00:19:25.472 --> 00:19:29.992
So she either says, yes, sir, and obeys a direct order, or you smack her in the mouth.

00:19:30.000 --> 00:19:32.840
and you drag her sorry ass down the sick bay and you make her take those pills.

00:19:39.500 --> 00:19:40.780
Well, I'm glad I'm not working for you.

00:19:43.884 --> 00:19:44.884
Damn right!

00:19:48.780 --> 00:19:49.780
So do I have to...

00:19:50.572 --> 00:19:51.572
Smack you in the mouth.

00:19:51.660 --> 00:19:52.020
Lieutenant.

00:19:54.892 --> 00:19:56.892
No sir, I'll take my pills.

00:19:57.996 --> 00:19:58.496
No.

00:20:02.720 --> 00:20:03.260
Carry on.

00:20:05.840 --> 00:20:07.560
Pilots, you're ready to run for flight briefing.

00:20:13.960 --> 00:20:14.240
What?

00:20:32.840 --> 00:20:33.080
Yeah.

00:21:13.310 --> 00:21:14.450
Two, three, eight, complete.

00:21:14.920 --> 00:21:15.740
Start the clock.

00:21:18.060 --> 00:21:20.270
Minutes, mark.

00:21:22.480 --> 00:21:26.850
All civilian ships present and strike my last.

00:21:27.740 --> 00:21:29.980
One civilian ship missing and unaccounted...

00:21:30.000 --> 00:21:59.980
force, sir. Which one? The Olympic Carrier, commercial passenger vessel. Were they left behind? I think I accounted for all civilian ships before we left, sir. You think? Did you or didn't you? They're not logged in, sir. I think they may have been left behind. How many people aboard ship? 1,345 souls, sir. You're telling me we left over 1,300 people to die?

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:01.160
at the hands of the Cylon.

00:22:01.340 --> 00:22:03.250
It may not have been her fault, sir.

00:22:04.150 --> 00:22:05.530
It may have simply been a navigational error

00:22:05.530 --> 00:22:06.630
and they jumped to the wrong coordinates,

00:22:06.930 --> 00:22:08.910
or the Cylons may have destroyed the ship before they jumped.

00:22:09.130 --> 00:22:10.490
Fifty other things may have happened.

00:22:10.610 --> 00:22:12.970
The point is, we don't know what the hell did happen.

00:22:19.250 --> 00:22:20.050
Yes, we're tired.

00:22:20.860 --> 00:22:21.860
Yes, there's no relief.

00:22:22.620 --> 00:22:27.080
Yes, the Cylons keep coming after us time after time after time.

00:22:27.320 --> 00:22:29.960
And yes, we are still expected to do our...

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:41.510
You make mistakes, people die.

00:22:45.040 --> 00:22:46.260
There aren't many of us left.

00:23:23.550 --> 00:23:24.090
Yes.

00:23:31.400 --> 00:23:34.670
But first, where's the doctor that's supposed to be on board?

00:23:34.750 --> 00:23:35.190
What's his name?

00:23:36.400 --> 00:23:37.120
Dr. Amrach.

00:23:37.400 --> 00:23:40.830
Yes, Dr. Amrach.

00:23:49.350 --> 00:23:50.290
He was on the Olympic carrier.

00:23:57.700 --> 00:23:58.960
God is watching out for you guys.

00:24:04.860 --> 00:24:15.820
The universe is a vast and complex system. Coincidental, serendipitous events are bound to occur. Indeed, they're to be expected. It's part of the pattern, part of the plan.

00:24:16.060 --> 00:24:21.460
Dr. Amorak posed a threat to you. Now he's gone, logic says there's a connection.

00:24:24.360 --> 00:24:26.700
Connection, maybe. But not God.

00:24:28.790 --> 00:24:29.430
There is no God.

00:24:30.090 --> 00:24:32.010
or God, singular or plural.

00:24:32.190 --> 00:24:35.690
There are no large, invisible men, or women, for that matter, in the sky,

00:24:35.810 --> 00:24:38.770
taking a personal interest in the fortunes of Gaius Baltar.

00:24:39.720 --> 00:24:44.090
Be careful. That which God gives, he can also take away.

00:24:52.110 --> 00:24:52.590
Fifteen seconds.

00:25:00.120 --> 00:25:01.100
Maybe this time.

00:25:01.420 --> 00:25:13.580
Try this.

00:25:15.380 --> 00:25:16.100
No enemy contacts.

00:25:18.540 --> 00:25:19.420
Keep the clock running.

00:25:28.030 --> 00:25:28.690
Think we wait.

00:26:01.440 --> 00:26:02.220
Get me the president.

00:26:09.980 --> 00:26:10.680
Why this time?

00:26:13.240 --> 00:26:14.440
Was it something that you did?

00:26:15.010 --> 00:26:17.290
We had a new plan, but we didn't have time to implement it yet.

00:26:17.970 --> 00:26:20.070
Well, we lost that ship during the last cycle.

00:26:20.210 --> 00:26:23.340
The Olympic carrier, did that have something to do with it?

00:26:24.320 --> 00:26:24.680
Possibly.

00:26:32.910 --> 00:26:33.510
Are you there?

00:26:34.920 --> 00:26:35.990
Yeah, I'm here.

00:26:38.600 --> 00:26:39.260
What do we do now?

00:26:39.680 --> 00:26:41.700
Commander, I've got people on the verge over here.

00:26:43.310 --> 00:26:44.630
We're gonna go to condition two.

00:26:45.780 --> 00:26:46.900
Take advantage of this time.

00:26:48.420 --> 00:26:51.640
How long do we?

00:26:52.200 --> 00:26:52.560
A day.

00:26:53.220 --> 00:26:54.000
At condition two.

00:26:54.880 --> 00:26:56.560
I'm satisfied they're not gonna return.

00:26:57.900 --> 00:26:58.760
Military decision.

00:27:00.160 --> 00:27:18.340
It is, I know that, you're right, and I defer to your decision, and Commander, you are men, women, grateful I am for the job that they thank them for me.

00:27:20.660 --> 00:27:21.020
Thank you.

00:27:22.740 --> 00:27:23.080
Thank you.

00:27:28.890 --> 00:27:29.630
Contact Apollo.

00:27:30.510 --> 00:27:33.210
He's come to set up a combat patrol around the fleet.

00:27:33.990 --> 00:27:35.770
Order his other pilots to land immediately.

00:27:37.290 --> 00:27:38.810
All right, people, you heard the order.

00:27:40.160 --> 00:27:42.020
Boomer, Starbuck, warm up with me.

00:27:42.080 --> 00:27:43.200
We'll fly the first cab.

00:27:44.210 --> 00:27:47.210
I want everyone else back on Galactica and in their rack.

00:27:47.990 --> 00:27:48.710
We are a rotation.

00:27:51.930 --> 00:27:55.270
I'm being chosen to sit in my cockpit for the next three hours, but...

00:27:55.270 --> 00:27:56.070
But why you?

00:27:57.640 --> 00:27:58.380
Take a guess.

00:27:59.500 --> 00:27:59.960
Because I'm on...

00:28:00.680 --> 00:28:04.760
You got it, this patrol is 100% stimulated.

00:28:05.400 --> 00:28:08.300
Does anyone else feel like you're fucking ants crawling behind their eyeballs?

00:28:09.410 --> 00:28:10.840
Hey, how about you, Boomer?

00:28:12.060 --> 00:28:14.900
Doc tells me you're holding up better than anybody in the squadron.

00:28:15.460 --> 00:28:16.640
I'm tired like everybody else.

00:28:16.820 --> 00:28:17.820
I've never seen it.

00:28:18.020 --> 00:28:19.020
It's because she's a Cylon.

00:28:19.630 --> 00:28:21.890
You're just gonna make me come over there and kick your ass, aren't you?

00:28:22.460 --> 00:28:26.120
Okay, okay, let's set up a patrol here before somebody gets hurt.

00:28:28.130 --> 00:28:28.690
Follow me.

00:28:36.750 --> 00:28:42.090
Oh, Blower's ragtime does sound awfully sweet right about you.

00:28:42.170 --> 00:28:42.710
You deserve it.

00:28:45.340 --> 00:28:46.040
You know?

00:28:46.920 --> 00:28:53.110
Truth is, all this has me feeling, well, more alive than I have in years.

00:28:57.160 --> 00:28:57.980
It's good to see you with that.

00:29:00.000 --> 00:29:04.950
start but i know there's a whole lot of people aboard this ship they wish you weren't feeling

